  "worked_solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+2 & =-4y-5 \\\\ -4y+2+4y & =-4y-5+4y \\\\ 2 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-4y+2=-4y-5$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+3 & =6y-1 \\\\ 6y+3-6y & =6y-1-6y \\\\ 3 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $6y+3=6y-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-7 & =2y+1 \\\\ 5y-7-2y+7 & =2y+1-2y+7 \\\\ 3y & =8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $5y-7=2y+1$ has the unique solution $y=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
